blocks.en:
Figure 9 highlights three characteristic behaviors that emerged during the interaction:
a hider builds cover by moving a barrier panel to block an entrance;
a seeker transports a ramp to an inner wall and climbs over it;
and, after an initial leap falls short, a seeker repositions the ramp closer to the wall and tries again.
These maneuvers demonstrate the agents’ ability to acquire and refine multi-step physical tool-use strategies
purely from neural-rendered first-person observations.

blocks.zh:
图9突出了相互作用过程中出现的三种特征行为:
a. 通过移动屏障面板来堵住入口来建立掩体;
寻求者将斜坡运送到内墙上并爬上它;
并且,在最初的一跃落空后,一个寻求者将坡道重新定位到更靠近墙上的位置并再次尝试.
这些操作表明代理人有能力获取和完善多步骤的物理工具使用战略
纯粹来自神经上的第一人称观测.
